  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.intro.title": "Pokémon Habitats",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.intro": "Pokémon in a pasture live in a habitat: the space they can reach around the Pasture Block, up to 10 blocks. Walls and fences close it.\n\nBuild it to their liking and they will be happy.",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.see.title": "Seeing the habitat",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.see": "Sneak + right-click your Pokémon and press the house button.\n\nOr sneak + right-click a pastured Pokémon holding the Pokédex.\n\nThe report shows up in the chat.",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.comfort.title": "Comfort",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.comfort": "Happy: green sparkles.\nComfortable.\nNeutral.\nUncomfortable: tears.\n\nWhat they like counts, what they dislike gets in the way, and a cramped pasture too. Pokémon with two types are happy if one of them is.",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.temperament.title": "Temperament",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.temperament": "It comes from the nature.\n\nHomebodies barely leave home. Explorers roam far. Everyone comes back at bedtime; nocturnal ones in the morning.\n\nOne that can't find its way back gets sad for a while.",
  "cobblemon_ecosystems.guide.likes": "Likes:",
